// Deep groove ball bearing 608, 8 x 22 x 7 mm, shielded on both faces:
// the outer and inner steel rings and the shields between them. Its axis
// along z, a face at z = 0, centered on the origin.
// https://www.electrokit.com/en/kullager-skf-8mm-dim-8x22x7
//
// From SKF's figures for the open 608, as Electrokit lists them: 8 x 22 x 7 mm,
// dynamic load rating 3.45 kN, static 1.37 kN, 12.1 g. A shielded 608-2Z has
// the same size and ratings; a sealed 608-2RS1 is rated lower (about 2 kN
// dynamic), as SKF's seals cost it room.
// The bore, outside diameter and width are ISO 15's for the designation,
// so any maker's 608 has them. The rings' section and the shields are
// drawn, not measured. To hold it in a printed part, `bearing_seat.c2f`
// cuts its pocket.

// @description Deep groove ball bearing 608, 8 mm bore, 22 mm outside, 7 mm
// @description wide: the bearing of skateboard wheels, fidget spinners and 3D
// @description printers' idlers: the cheapest and easiest to find.
// @spec bearing: deep groove ball bearing, single row, 608 (SKF 608)
// @spec bore: 8 mm
// @spec outside diameter: 22 mm
// @spec width: 7 mm
// @spec dynamic load: 3.45 kN
// @spec static load: 1.37 kN
// @spec mass: 12.1 g
// @source https://www.electrokit.com/en/kullager-skf-8mm-dim-8x22x7 SKF 608 at Electrokit (dimensions, load ratings, mass)

use <lib/ball_bearing.c2f>

module bearing_608() {
    ball_bearing(8, 22, 7);
}

bearing_608();
